a del tratamiento de la diabetes.", "MANUAL SEEN DE ENDOCRINOLOGÍA:", "PHARMACOLOGIC APPROACHES TO GLYCEMIC TREATMENT:A set of standards for medical care in diabetes that outlines pharmacologic approaches to glycemic treatment.", "UK PROSPECTIVE DIABETES STUDY GROUP:A research group that conducted the UK Prospective Diabetes Study, which compared intensive blood-glucose control with conventional treatment in type 2 diabetes patients.", "INSULIN INFUSION:A method of delivering insulin continuously through a subcutaneous device, compared to multiple daily injections.", "TYPE 2 DIABETES:Type 2 diabetes is a chronic condition that significantly impacts the body's ability to process blood sugar (glucose). It is often associated with obesity and various lifestyle factors, including diet. This form of diabetes can arise when the body becomes resistant to insulin or when the pancreas fails to produce sufficient insulin. Research has indicated that dietary influences play a crucial role in managing this condition, with studies suggesting that higher dietary fiber intake may lower the risk of developing Type 2 diabetes. Management of the condition can sometimes be achieved through lifestyle changes and the use of oral medications.", "GLYCEMIC CONTROL:Glycemic control refers to the management of blood glucose levels in individuals with diabetes, which is essential for preventing complications associated with the condition. This management often involves dietary adjustments and the use of medication to maintain optimal blood sugar levels. By effectively controlling glycemic levels, diabetic patients can reduce the risk of serious health issues and improve their overall well-being.", "LIPOHYPERTROPHY:A condition that can occur in diabetes patients due to repeated insulin injections in the same area, leading to erratic insulin absorption.", "LIPOATROPHY:A condition characterized by the loss of fat tissue, which can also affect insulin absorption in diabetes patients.", "GÓMEZ-HUELGAS R:Gómez-Huelgas R is a researcher involved in the consensus document on the treatment of type 2 diabetes in patients with chronic kidney disease.", "MARTÍNEZ-CASTELAO A:Martínez-Castelao A is a researcher who contributed to the consensus document regarding diabetes treatment in patients with chronic kidney disease.", "ARTOLA S:Artola S is a researcher who is part of the group that developed the consensus document on diabetes treatment."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}